# Measurement evidence and review artefacts.
#
# Large binary or derived outputs -- about 1.9 GB here: 212 MB of source crops,
# 290 MB of repair previews, 289 MB of visual audits, 46 MB of staged owner
# output. They are reproducible from the pipeline and the owner's standing
# instruction is not to commit binary assets. They are deliberately untracked
# rather than absent: they exist on the working machine and still need a storage
# answer, so do not delete them to "clean up" a worktree.
public/data/city-expansion/evidence/
public/data/facade-repair-preview/
review-data/visual-audits/
review-data/staged-owner-output/
.flash/

# NOTE: public/data/city-expansion/releases/ is deliberately NOT ignored.
# Releases are served game data, not evidence -- current.json points at one and
# the game fetches its tiles -- and 64 of them are already tracked. The fourteen
# district releases of 36-48 MB each are untracked only because nobody decided
# whether to carry that weight in git; that is an open owner decision, not a
# rule. A fresh checkout is self-consistent today because the committed
# current.json points at a release that is committed.

# Review galleries and evaluation contact sheets: rendered PNG/JPG comparisons,
# regenerated by their own scripts from data that is tracked. Binary assets, so
# they stay out per the owner's standing instruction.
public/data/city-expansion/evaluations/
public/data/district-materials/
public/data/facade-review-galleries/
review-data/case20-dormer-city-preview/
review-data/case22-gable-city-preview/
review-data/case24-gable-city-preview/
review-data/case25-flat-city-preview/
review-data/case25-source-correction/
review-data/building-source-comparison/

# Loop-status screenshots, regenerated by scripts/review/build-loop-status.ts.
public/canal-drive/loop-status/
# Full OSM building dumps from refresh — hundreds of MB; LoD1 tiles cover play.
public/data/extracts/*/buildings-osm.geojson
tmp/

# Local renders and preview harnesses (render:large-letter-craft writes here)
.tmp/
